  <abstract format="text/plain" language="en" script="Latn">Recommendation ITU-T K.44 seeks to establish fundamental test methods and criteria for the resistibility of telecommunication equipment to overvoltages and overcurrents.Overvoltages or overcurrents covered by this Recommendation include surges due to lightning on or near the line plant, short-term induction of alternating voltages from adjacent electric power lines or electrified railway systems, earth potential rise due to power faults and direct contacts between telecommunication lines and power lines.Major changes compared with the 2018 version of this Recommendation include:Corrigendum 1 adds the missing values for R1 and R2 in the key of Figure A.6.7-2. These values should be the same as the R1 and R2 values in the key of Figure A.6.7-5.</abstract>
